      "id": 16,
      "options": {
        "content": "### SecureFlow Observability Coverage & Follow-Up Scope\n\nThis dashboard visualizes all metrics currently emitted by the SecureFlow application at `/api/metrics/landing`:\n- **`secureflow_database_live`**: Database connectivity indicator (1 = Healthy, 0 = Degraded).\n- **`secureflow_scans_total`**: Total completed vulnerability and policy scans.\n- **`secureflow_repositories_total`**: Total monitored repositories.\n- **`secureflow_prs_total`**: Total pull requests evaluated.\n- **`secureflow_prs_passed_total` & `secureflow_prs_blocked_total`**: PR policy pass vs block outcomes.\n- **`secureflow_findings_total{type=\"...\"}`**: Security findings categorized by type (`secret`, `vulnerability`, `misconfig`).\n- **`secureflow_scan_duration_seconds`**: Average scan duration in seconds.\n\n---\n\n#### Follow-Up Metrics Backlog\nAs required by the zero-unemitted-metrics standard, the following metrics are tracked for upcoming emission in follow-up issues:\n1. **Queue Depth Telemetry** (`secureflow_queue_waiting_jobs`, `secureflow_queue_active_jobs`): Tracked in Redis BullMQ queues, to be exported in the Prometheus registry.\n2. **LLM Inference Provider Health** (`secureflow_llm_requests_total`, `secureflow_llm_errors_total`): Currently logged; to be exposed on the `/api/metrics/landing` Prometheus registry.\n3. **AI Circuit-Breaker State** (`secureflow_circuit_breaker_state`): State of model circuit-breakers (0=CLOSED, 1=HALF_OPEN, 2=OPEN).\n",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "10.0.0",
      "title": "Telemetry Coverage & Follow-Up Scope",
      "type": "text"
